<title>JAPAN: Mazda Motor hits 1997 high.</title>
<headline>Mazda Motor hits 1997 high.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Mazda Motor Corp rose to a new high for the calendar year on Tuesday morning, attracting investors as a laggard in the automobile sector, traders said.</p>
<p>The shares briefly touched 418 yen, the highest level so far in 1997.</p>
<p>At 0149 GMT, they traded 15 yen higher at 415. Volume was 1.89 million shares, making the firm the sixth-heaviest traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.  </p>
<p>&quot;People are after Mazda shares, which have lagged behind in the sector,&quot; said a broker at a &quot;Big Four&quot; securities house.</p>
